  "finalCues": [
    {
      "verse": 1,
      "text": "When you sit to dine with a ruler, note well what is before you,",
      "start": 4.024,
      "end": 8.259
    },
    {
      "verse": 2,
      "text": "and put a knife to your throat if you are given to gluttony.",
      "start": 8.64,
      "end": 12.06
    },
    {
      "verse": 3,
      "text": "Do not crave his delicacies, for that food is deceptive.",
      "start": 12.5,
      "end": 16.552
    },
    {
      "verse": 4,
      "text": "Do not wear yourself out to get rich; do not trust your own cleverness.",
      "start": 19.12,
      "end": 24.21
    },
    {
      "verse": 5,
      "text": "Cast but a glance at riches, and they are gone, for they will surely sprout wings and fly off to the sky like an eagle.",
      "start": 24.52,
      "end": 31.55
    },
    {
      "verse": 6,
      "text": "Do not eat the food of a begrudging host, do not crave his delicacies;",
      "start": 33.7,
      "end": 38.019
    },
    {
      "verse": 7,
      "text": "for he is the kind of person who is always thinking about the cost.“Eat and drink,” he says to you, but his heart is not with you.",
      "start": 38.22,
      "end": 46.98
    },
    {
      "verse": 8,
      "text": "You will vomit up the little you have eaten and will have wasted your compliments.",
      "start": 47.46,
      "end": 52.168
    },
    {
      "verse": 9,
      "text": "Do not speak to fools, for they will scorn your prudent words.",
      "start": 54.26,
      "end": 58.44
    },
    {
      "verse": 10,
      "text": "Do not move an ancient boundary stone or encroach on the fields of the fatherless,",
      "start": 60.46,
      "end": 65.48
    },
    {
      "verse": 11,
      "text": "for their Defender is strong; he will take up their case against you.",
      "start": 65.6,
      "end": 69.672
    },
    {
      "verse": 12,
      "text": "Apply your heart to instruction and your ears to words of knowledge.",
      "start": 72.1,
      "end": 76.584
    },
    {
      "verse": 13,
      "text": "Do not withhold discipline from a child; if you punish them with the rod, they will not die.",
      "start": 78.84,
      "end": 84.424
    },
    {
      "verse": 14,
      "text": "Punish them with the rod and save them from death.",
      "start": 84.7,
      "end": 88.2
    },
    {
      "verse": 15,
      "text": "My son, if your heart is wise, then my heart will be glad indeed;",
      "start": 91.3,
      "end": 95.839
    },
    {
      "verse": 16,
      "text": "my inmost being will rejoice when your lips speak what is right.",
      "start": 96.22,
      "end": 100.488
    },
    {
      "verse": 17,
      "text": "Do not let your heart envy sinners, but always be zealous for the fear of the LORD.",
      "start": 103.44,
      "end": 109.064
    },
    {
      "verse": 18,
      "text": "There is surely a future hope for you, and your hope will not be cut off.",
      "start": 109.52,
      "end": 113.992
    },
    {
      "verse": 19,
      "text": "Listen, my son, and be wise, and set your heart on the right path:",
      "start": 116.8,
      "end": 121.259
    },
    {
      "verse": 20,
      "text": "Do not join those who drink too much wine or gorge themselves on meat,",
      "start": 121.52,
      "end": 126.219
    },
    {
      "verse": 21,
      "text": "for drunkards and gluttons become poor, and drowsiness clothes them in rags.",
      "start": 126.5,
      "end": 132.168
    },
    {
      "verse": 22,
      "text": "Listen to your father, who gave you life, and do not despise your mother when she is old.",
      "start": 135.361,
      "end": 140.456
    },
    {
      "verse": 23,
      "text": "Buy the truth and do not sell it— wisdom, instruction and insight as well.",
      "start": 140.88,
      "end": 146.088
    },
    {
      "verse": 24,
      "text": "The father of a righteous child has great joy; a man who fathers a wise son rejoices in him.",
      "start": 146.64,
      "end": 153.224
    },
    {
      "verse": 25,
      "text": "May your father and mother rejoice; may she who gave you birth be joyful!",
      "start": 153.78,
      "end": 159.298
    },
    {
      "verse": 26,
      "text": "My son, give me your heart and let your eyes delight in my ways,",
      "start": 162.181,
      "end": 166.32
    },
    {
      "verse": 27,
      "text": "for an adulterous woman is a deep pit, and a wayward wife is a narrow well.",
      "start": 166.4,
      "end": 171.784
    },
    {
      "verse": 28,
      "text": "Like a bandit she lies in wait and multiplies the unfaithful among men.",
      "start": 172.34,
      "end": 177.544
    },
    {
      "verse": 29,
      "text": "Who has woe? Who has sorrow? Who has strife? Who has complaints? Who has needless bruises? Who has bloodshot eyes?",
      "start": 180.44,
      "end": 191.112
    },
    {
      "verse": 30,
      "text": "Those who linger over wine, who go to sample bowls of mixed wine.",
      "start": 191.74,
      "end": 196.36
    },
    {
      "verse": 31,
      "text": "Do not gaze at wine when it is red, when it sparkles in the cup, when it goes down smoothly!",
      "start": 196.78,
      "end": 202.728
    },
    {
      "verse": 32,
      "text": "In the end it bites like a snake and poisons like a viper.",
      "start": 202.86,
      "end": 206.64
    },
    {
      "verse": 33,
      "text": "Your eyes will see strange sights, and your mind will imagine confusing things.",
      "start": 206.96,
      "end": 212.2
    },
    {
      "verse": 34,
      "text": "You will be like one sleeping on the high seas, lying on top of the rigging.",
      "start": 212.28,
      "end": 216.68
    },
    {
      "verse": 35,
      "text": "“They hit me,” you will say, “but I’m not hurt! They beat me, but I don’t feel it! When will I wake up so I can find another drink?”",
      "start": 216.85,
      "end": 226.632
    }
  ],
